shown as `UNSOURCED` rather than inferred.

## Executive summary

NuScale develops small modular nuclear reactors and is trying to move from
engineering and licensing work into commercial reactor-module sales and services.
Its strongest evidence is NRC approval of its six-unit 77 MWe design, substantial
cash and investments, and an exclusive commercialization relationship with
ENTRA1. **[Source: SEC Form 10-K, Business / Regulatory Approvals, page UNSOURCED;
SEC Form 10-Q, Business / Liquidity and Capital Resources, page UNSOURCED; call
date: UNSOURCED](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1822966/000182296626000018/smr-20251231.htm)**

The counterevidence is that revenue remains very small, losses and operating cash
use remain substantial, and the company raised capital through significant share
issuance. **[Source: SEC Form 10-Q, Statements of Operations / Statements of Cash
Flows / Loss Per Share, pages UNSOURCED; call date: UNSOURCED](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1822966/000182296626000085/smr-20260630.htm)**

**My judgment:** Watch-defer rather than initiate a base-case position until the
commercial thesis is supported by binding, economically specific customer
commitments and a credible path from cash burn to positive operating economics.

## What NuScale is and how it makes money

NuScale develops and commercializes small modular nuclear reactors. **[Source: SEC
Form 10-K, Business, page UNSOURCED; call date: UNSOURCED](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1822966/000182296626000018/smr-20251231.htm)**

Its core product, the NuScale Power Module (NPM), is a 77 MWe light-water reactor
module. **[Source: SEC Form 10-K, Business and Regulatory Discussion, page
UNSOURCED; call date: UNSOURCED](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1822966/000182296626000018/smr-20251231.htm)**

The company reports that current revenue comes mainly from engineering and
licensing services and fees. Future revenue is expected from NPM sales and
installation, startup and testing, nuclear fuel, and refueling services. **[Source:
SEC Form 10-K, Business and Revenue Recognition, page UNSOURCED; call date:
UNSOURCED](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1822966/000182296626000018/smr-20251231.htm)**

**Plain-English implication:** NuScale is not yet a mature utility or equipment
manufacturer with recurring fleet revenue; the investment case depends on
converting its technology and licensing progress into financed, profitable
deployments. **[Source: UNSOURCED — interpretation based on the supplied report; call date: UNSOURCED]**

## What is good

- The NRC finalized approval of the six-unit 77 MWe design in May 2025. **[Source:
  SEC Form 10-K, Regulatory Approvals, page UNSOURCED; call date: UNSOURCED](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1822966/000182296626000018/smr-20251231.htm)**
- At June 30, 2026, SMR reported $766.5 million of cash, $305.7 million of
  short-term investments, $820.8 million of investments, and no debt. **[Source:
  SEC Form 10-Q, Liquidity and Capital Resources, page UNSOURCED; call date:
  UNSOURCED](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1822966/000182296626000085/smr-20260630.htm)**
- ENTRA1 is described as NuScale's exclusive global strategic partner for
  commercialization and development. **[Source: SEC Form 10-Q, Business, page
  UNSOURCED; call date: UNSOURCED](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1822966/000182296626000085/smr-20260630.htm)**

**My judgment:** Regulatory approval, a substantial liquidity cushion, and a
commercialization partner give SMR a credible platform from which a successful
nuclear-deployment business could develop.

## What is bad

- Q2 2026 revenue was $75,000 and six-month 2026 revenue was $640,000. **[Source:
  SEC Form 10-Q, Statements of Operations, page UNSOURCED; call date:
  UNSOURCED](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1822966/000182296626000085/smr-20260630.htm)**
- Six-month 2026 net loss was $96.7 million and operating cash use was $372.9
  million. **[Source: SEC Form 10-Q, Statements of Operations and Cash Flows, page
  UNSOURCED; call date: UNSOURCED](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1822966/000182296626000085/smr-20260630.htm)**
- SMR issued 89.7 million Class A shares for approximately $1.0 billion gross
  proceeds during the first half of 2026. **[Source: SEC Form 10-Q, Loss Per Share /
  ATM Program, page UNSOURCED; call date: UNSOURCED](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1822966/000182296626000085/smr-20260630.htm)**

**My judgment:** The company has not yet demonstrated recurring commercial
revenue, positive operating cash flow, or protection against material dilution.

## Challenges, risks, and advantages

The filing identifies competition from traditional baseload, renewables,
long-duration storage, other nuclear reactors, and other SMR technologies. **[Source:
SEC Form 10-K, Competition, page UNSOURCED; call date: UNSOURCED](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1822966/000182296626000018/smr-20251231.htm)**

The latest 10-Q says there were no material changes to the risk factors in the
2025 10-K. **[Source: SEC Form 10-Q, Item 1A Risk Factors, page UNSOURCED; call
date: UNSOURCED](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1822966/000182296626000085/smr-20260630.htm)**

Management states that ENTRA1 retains discretion over whether to proceed with
commercialization opportunities and that binding customer contracts are still
needed. **[Source: SEC Form 10-Q, Business, page UNSOURCED; call date:
UNSOURCED](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1822966/000182296626000085/smr-20260630.htm)**

- **Advantages (my judgment):** NRC approval, modular design, potential demand
  for carbon-free firm power, and strong liquidity relative to near-term needs.
- **Challenges (my judgment):** Converting non-binding interest into profitable
  orders, managing nuclear construction and supply-chain execution, funding
  ongoing losses, and limiting dilution.

