## Management outlook

Management says it is transitioning from research and development toward
commercialization, focusing on commercial contracts and production readiness.
**[Source: SEC Form 10-Q, Liquidity and Capital Resources, page UNSOURCED; call
date: UNSOURCED](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1822966/000182296626000085/smr-20260630.htm)**

Management says existing cash, investments, and expected capital-market access
should satisfy cash requirements for the next 12 months and beyond. **[Source: SEC
Form 10-Q, Liquidity and Capital Resources, page UNSOURCED; call date:
UNSOURCED](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1822966/000182296626000085/smr-20260630.htm)**

**My interpretation:** This is a liquidity statement, not a revenue or profit
forecast; it lowers near-term funding pressure but does not establish that the
business will earn an acceptable return on capital.

